# Runtime state the services write beside themselves: the company record,
# the fleet room, the outbox, the read marks, and the session table.
#
# Matched by PREFIX, not by name. The named list that used to be here was
# defeated by an ordinary rename: HLL -> GMN moved every one of these to a
# gmn- name, none of which was listed, and the whole set — including 38
# live bearer tokens — was committed to a public repo before anyone
# noticed. A glob would have held through the rename. This one does.
hll-*.json
hll-*.json.tmp
hll-*.jsonl
hll-*.jsonl.tmp
gmn-*.json
gmn-*.json.tmp
gmn-*.jsonl
gmn-*.jsonl.tmp

# screenshots from tools/shots.js — generated, not source
.shots/


# .NET intermediates for the telemetry adapter. obj/ and bin/ are rebuilt by
# `dotnet build` every time and churn on every compile — two of them were
# already showing as modified with nobody having touched the source.
# hll-telemetry-adapter.exe stays tracked on purpose: telemetry-bridge.js
# spawns it at runtime, so a clone without it cannot read the game.
telemetry-adapter/obj/
telemetry-adapter/bin/
*.pdb

.fake
